  "provenance": {
    "pattern": "roots reggae and dub: the one drop — kick and rim together on the third beat and nothing on the one — with the skank chopping the chord on two and four and a bass line that walks around the root",
    "knowledge": "public knowledge of the genre: the pattern as drummers, producers and tutorials commonly write it; no recording was sampled, transcribed from audio or mined",
    "note": "One bar: the kick and a cross-stick land together on beat three (step 8), the hats tick the eighths with the offbeat lighter, the skank is a short triad on two and four. The bass is a two-bar melodic line inside a fifth that leaves the one empty, as roots bass lines do. Played under the Downtempo key, whose band is the slowest with drums (95-105): a one drop wants 70-80, where no band is."
  }
